#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087450 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f88c1deb-cd11-5b68-b90b-2d8edfae2469" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Equation of a Wide Ellipse"}] :question/id #uuid "446ea007-1ff4-5023-8e3f-7f00eb0fb2d0" :question/math-academy-id "e-5071" :question/problem "What is the equation of the ellipse given below?\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039348/assets/6d2ba3fba1a05a841a486553ea3a52d6f3797974630420ad79ae50f4c6f5bc15.png)" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the equation of an ellipse centered at the origin with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{x^2}{a^2}+\\dfrac{y^2}{b^2}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nHere, the horizontal radius has length $a=5$ and the vertical radius has length $b=3.$ Therefore, the equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{{5}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{3}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{25}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087451 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "de557d1d-5f27-50e3-bcba-22b21f83267f" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Equation of a Tall Ellipse"}] :question/id #uuid "af56117c-65e0-5f12-9780-7a95e6be829e" :question/math-academy-id "e-5072" :question/problem "What is the equation of the ellipse given below?\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039348/assets/3e8d5ed4bf055960b50e046c0688a3c4cc69907ebb1209bb9658ac4bcba48ffe.png)" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the equation of an ellipse centered at the origin with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{x^2}{a^2}+\\dfrac{y^2}{b^2}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nHere, the horizontal radius has length $a=2$ and the vertical radius has length $b=4.$ Therefore, the equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{{2}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{4}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{16} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087452 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4e43e393-8752-58bc-b87c-b72f679cbfd9" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Lengths of the Major and Minor Axes Given the Equation of an Ellipse"}] :question/id #uuid "b7c94673-f847-5977-9b9f-8d235ea42eb2" :question/math-academy-id "e-5073" :question/problem "What are the lengths of the major and minor axes of an ellipse with equation $\\dfrac{x^2}{36} + \\dfrac{y^2}{25} = 1?$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the equation of an ellipse centered at the origin with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{x^2}{a^2}+\\dfrac{y^2}{b^2}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nIn the given equation, we have $a^2=36$ and $b^2=25.$\n\n- Since $a^2=36,$ the length of the horizontal radius must be $a=\\sqrt{36} = 6.$\n\n- Since $b^2=25,$ the length of the vertical radius must be $b=\\sqrt{25} = 5.$\n\nSo the semi-major axis has length $a=6,$ and the semi-minor axis has length $b=5.$\n\nTherefore, the major axis has length $2a = 2 \\cdot 6 = 12,$ and the minor axis has length $2b = 2 \\cdot 5 =10.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186302588 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "de557d1d-5f27-50e3-bcba-22b21f83267f" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Equation of a Tall Ellipse"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "31bd6c00-f798-5f52-8846-d0354e446d46" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{8}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302590} {:answer/id #uuid "0f790dec-57a6-50e2-ae78-aecfd1e526bc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{1}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{16}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302591} {:answer/id #uuid "3018ea92-63a7-573e-b157-ec5f717b1254" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{16}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{1}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302592} {:answer/id #uuid "1de88b45-c080-5a50-be90-5f0c5be697c5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{1}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302593} {:answer/id #uuid "3569ca0f-f09b-58e7-b673-c4e366db8821" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{1}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302594}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0f790dec-57a6-50e2-ae78-aecfd1e526bc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{1}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{16}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302591} :answer-field/id #uuid "12fc5801-5621-5551-975d-5ccdd051d75a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302589}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a6b7394b-01c9-52bb-809f-2cab825b18da" :question/math-academy-id "q-115129" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039348/assets/c71a52cc148f8ce4a23a2fb2005757c9d141d3caf05586d8fb5122f591dc7474.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the ellipse given above?" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the equation of an ellipse centered at the origin with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nHere, the horizontal radius has length $a=1$ and the vertical radius has length $b=4.$ Therefore, the equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{{1}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{4}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{1}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{16} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186267445 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "de557d1d-5f27-50e3-bcba-22b21f83267f" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Equation of a Tall Ellipse"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "23cd513c-0f75-5c1f-b46c-45e80c3719c6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{3}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{6}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267447} {:answer/id #uuid "6d7d5c88-1459-536c-b6da-74258ee639fc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{36}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267448} {:answer/id #uuid "2da80e4f-bebd-5d21-bbbf-0441a5bd9e98" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{6}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{3}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267449} {:answer/id #uuid "8bd22e77-097f-5aed-a9f0-69d727c4148f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{9}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{36}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267450} {:answer/id #uuid "da0b1065-0ffd-54b2-a18a-78cfcc4ec9da" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{6}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{12}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267451}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8bd22e77-097f-5aed-a9f0-69d727c4148f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{9}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{36}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267450} :answer-field/id #uuid "feb2af5e-054b-59f7-be64-d428bf579b78" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267446}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "20f799f9-37ea-5b3e-b820-5abed8180539" :question/math-academy-id "q-16451" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039348/assets/6116ecf00a26d9828b238879b61385c1296f33ff863dbb8337a3b22be5981f10.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the ellipse given above?" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the equation of an ellipse centered at the origin with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nHere, the horizontal radius has length $a=3$ and the vertical radius has length $b=6.$ Therefore, the equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{{3}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{6}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{9}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{36} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186302595 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4e43e393-8752-58bc-b87c-b72f679cbfd9" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Lengths of the Major and Minor Axes Given the Equation of an Ellipse"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1722f41a-afa9-525e-a1fd-62d5499b043c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$2\\sqrt{2}$ and $\\sqrt{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302597} {:answer/id #uuid "028101b6-364f-568f-8d72-b8457b6b641e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$8$ and $4$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302598} {:answer/id #uuid "34b74a26-5ad4-57a6-a41d-060a064812a6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$4$ and $2\\sqrt{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302599} {:answer/id #uuid "9246fb75-7836-569e-b02b-1f0dd0711b28" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$4$ and $2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302600} {:answer/id #uuid "f7db46ca-fb33-5454-a0e1-0cadf0330499" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$2\\sqrt{2}$ and $2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302601}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "34b74a26-5ad4-57a6-a41d-060a064812a6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$4$ and $2\\sqrt{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302599} :answer-field/id #uuid "0523d0ad-16cf-57cf-90d1-c281bfc83b91" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302596}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "de7c911d-465c-5e7a-89aa-81a0a052648b" :question/math-academy-id "q-16452" :question/problem "What are the lengths of the major and minor axes of an ellipse with equation \n$\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}=1?$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the equation of an ellipse centered at the origin with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nIn the given equation, we have ${a}^{2}=4$ and ${b}^{2}=2.$\n\n- Since ${a}^{2}=4,$ the length of the horizontal radius must be $a=\\sqrt{4}=2.$\n\n- Since ${b}^{2}=2,$ the length of the vertical radius must be $b=\\sqrt{2}.$\n\nSo the semi-major axis has length $a=2,$ and the semi-minor axis has length $b=\\sqrt{2}.$\n\nTherefore, the major axis has length $2a=2\\cdot 2=4,$ and the minor axis has length $2b=2\\cdot \\sqrt{2}=2\\sqrt{2}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186302602 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f88c1deb-cd11-5b68-b90b-2d8edfae2469" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Equation of a Wide Ellipse"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "793eab90-288c-5025-9f72-bd8efe019373" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x^2}{64}+\\frac{y^2}{20.25}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302604} {:answer/id #uuid "f0d6fef3-08ed-5337-84c2-0832a2cd81b9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x^2}{8}+\\frac{y^2}{4.5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302605}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "793eab90-288c-5025-9f72-bd8efe019373" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x^2}{64}+\\frac{y^2}{20.25}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302604} :answer-field/id #uuid "de883f47-5217-5724-8d3f-ca5ad38dcdec" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302603}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a238f27d-73c6-5f1a-903f-f75b1e29e25b" :question/math-academy-id "q-279125" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039348/assets/e1bfe4335b41f14dce0f3d614ca108a4d6d83c4aa65fc44f169431175c82f1b5.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the ellipse given above?\n\n{{field-1}}$=1$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the equation of an ellipse centered at the origin with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nHere, the horizontal radius has length $a=8$ and the vertical radius has length $b=\\frac{9}{2}.$ Therefore, the equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{{8}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{(\\frac{9}{2})}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{64}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{(\\frac{81}{4})} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{64}+\\frac{4{y}^{2}}{81} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186302606 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f88c1deb-cd11-5b68-b90b-2d8edfae2469" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Equation of a Wide Ellipse"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2aa45642-0521-51cd-b388-2f8d10af62b5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x^2}{72.25}+\\frac{y^2}{12.25}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302608}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2aa45642-0521-51cd-b388-2f8d10af62b5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x^2}{72.25}+\\frac{y^2}{12.25}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302608} :answer-field/id #uuid "714dfb41-290d-5d13-9fa0-9159e509b7db" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302607}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a1361ab6-806b-56de-924f-b7e320596a4f" :question/math-academy-id "q-279130" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039348/assets/1fcd12762c7b86e1d40813a747b75e1f9b21d83787824f5f48725ac9a1dddff6.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the ellipse given above?\n\n{{field-1}}$=1$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the equation of an ellipse centered at the origin with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nHere, the horizontal radius has length $a=\\frac{17}{2}$ and the vertical radius has length $b=\\frac{7}{2}.$ Therefore, the equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{{(\\frac{17}{2})}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{(\\frac{7}{2})}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{(\\frac{289}{4})}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{(\\frac{49}{4})} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{4{x}^{2}}{289}+\\frac{4{y}^{2}}{49} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186302609 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4e43e393-8752-58bc-b87c-b72f679cbfd9" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Lengths of the Major and Minor Axes Given the Equation of an Ellipse"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d49428e2-09f5-5fa2-832e-472caf401405" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302611}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d49428e2-09f5-5fa2-832e-472caf401405" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302611} :answer-field/id #uuid "617a7b14-a82c-57c4-9d97-989ab57e0c1e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302610} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "60bf746b-b736-5a8f-89ec-a28eb5121661" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302613}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "60bf746b-b736-5a8f-89ec-a28eb5121661" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302613} :answer-field/id #uuid "721f4a97-2e90-559a-8019-033fddefb719" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302612}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f3f5be58-b580-5f5b-b51d-181a795c844e" :question/math-academy-id "q-279172" :question/problem "For the ellipse $\\frac{{x}^{2}}{36}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{5}=1,$ find the lengths of its major and minor axes.\n\n$\\,$ The length of the major axis is \n{{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ The length of the minor axis is \n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "Remember that the equation of an ellipse centered at the origin with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nIn the given equation, we have ${a}^{2}=36$ and ${b}^{2}=5.$\n\n- Since ${a}^{2}=36,$ the length of the horizontal radius must be $a=\\sqrt{36}=6.$\n\n- Since ${b}^{2}=5,$ the length of the vertical radius must be $b=\\sqrt{5}.$\n\nThus, the semi-major axis has length $a=6,$ and the semi-minor axis has length $b=\\sqrt{5}.$\n\nTherefore, the major axis has length $2a=2\\cdot 6=12,$ and the minor axis has length $2b=2\\cdot \\sqrt{5}=2\\sqrt{5}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186302614 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4e43e393-8752-58bc-b87c-b72f679cbfd9" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Lengths of the Major and Minor Axes Given the Equation of an Ellipse"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ec3bd655-3364-5495-9679-0e145c9df1fa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302616} {:answer/id #uuid "c11b67ee-c12e-565b-9fc5-2eff5e0a6b19" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302617}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c11b67ee-c12e-565b-9fc5-2eff5e0a6b19" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302617} :answer-field/id #uuid "5ed18835-8117-5b30-ac45-d214f8df0f38" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302615} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7aea9913-6c57-50c3-b4d5-77599533139e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302619}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7aea9913-6c57-50c3-b4d5-77599533139e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302619} :answer-field/id #uuid "b4b37ddb-c852-5d0b-85bf-342941ca846c" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302618}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "97355673-c5e8-5526-b74b-524ac265b2d0" :question/math-academy-id "q-279174" :question/problem "For the ellipse $\\frac{{x}^{2}}{12}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}=1,$ find the lengths of its major and minor axes.\n\n$\\,$ The length of the major axis is \n{{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ The length of the minor axis is \n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "Remember that the equation of an ellipse centered at the origin with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nIn the given equation, we have ${a}^{2}=12$ and ${b}^{2}=9.$\n\n- Since ${a}^{2}=12,$ the length of the horizontal radius must be $a=\\sqrt{12}=2\\sqrt{3}.$\n\n- Since ${b}^{2}=9,$ the length of the vertical radius must be $b=\\sqrt{9}=3.$\n\nThus, the semi-major axis has length $a=2\\sqrt{3},$ and the semi-minor axis has length $b=3.$\n\nTherefore, the major axis has length $2a=2\\cdot 2\\sqrt{3}=4\\sqrt{3},$ and the minor axis has length $2b=2\\cdot 3=6.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186302620 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "de557d1d-5f27-50e3-bcba-22b21f83267f" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Equation of a Tall Ellipse"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4102dd04-292b-5aa0-be43-eaca3f7b98e9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{5}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302622} {:answer/id #uuid "341d6331-272c-53ad-8d6c-f724841c85a1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{5}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302623} {:answer/id #uuid "d9221f3e-391d-51e6-8eeb-3c9323e17425" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{25}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302624} {:answer/id #uuid "c0b7fde4-ca32-5996-a1e5-665eb886edf8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{25}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302625} {:answer/id #uuid "062d034f-943a-5896-a335-90c666e01815" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{10}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302626}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c0b7fde4-ca32-5996-a1e5-665eb886edf8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{25}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302625} :answer-field/id #uuid "30ca1e55-10d3-51da-aece-ec767a7ef1d4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302621}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "60ed3df5-f374-5da1-8a03-7183d44bf408" :question/math-academy-id "q-69893" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039348/assets/be8468d84e3820bd1e9181d31aa3a1b7d1a85c743020a69cb67fc3f601a88363.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the ellipse given above?" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the equation of an ellipse centered at the origin with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nHere, the horizontal radius has length $a=2$ and the vertical radius has length $b=5.$ Therefore, the equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{{2}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{5}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{25} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186267491 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f88c1deb-cd11-5b68-b90b-2d8edfae2469" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Equation of a Wide Ellipse"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0ec17315-ecea-5a46-86b9-10826fc86f8f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{4{y}^{2}}{9}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267493} {:answer/id #uuid "709bd1aa-6289-5f10-a063-81c1ac15b7ee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{9{y}^{2}}{4}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267494} {:answer/id #uuid "1bc5aca1-cf29-5761-be5f-7bdf0e50b9b7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{9}+\\frac{4{y}^{2}}{9}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267495} {:answer/id #uuid "3f96ca79-5e37-5709-a2c2-fb41f6a9e901" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{9}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267496} {:answer/id #uuid "4c823ea5-1ab4-51c8-9be9-6254583d5542" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{9}+\\frac{9{y}^{2}}{4}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267497}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1bc5aca1-cf29-5761-be5f-7bdf0e50b9b7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{9}+\\frac{4{y}^{2}}{9}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267495} :answer-field/id #uuid "5ab01a51-dea6-54fe-8d4a-a18973f2a125" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267492}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "75a4ea63-60ed-555d-b33c-9e409712e1e5" :question/math-academy-id "q-73619" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039348/assets/8637901efc126236b190e7012cf65a06be078cb21c3093eff39b927493000138.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the ellipse given above?" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the equation of an ellipse centered at the origin with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nHere, the horizontal radius has length $a=3$ and the vertical radius has length $b=1.5.$ Therefore, the equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{{3}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{1.5}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{{3}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{(\\frac{3}{2})}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{9}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{(\\frac{{3}^{2}}{{2}^{2}})} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{9}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{(\\frac{9}{4})} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{9}+\\frac{4{y}^{2}}{9} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186302627 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "de557d1d-5f27-50e3-bcba-22b21f83267f" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Equation of a Tall Ellipse"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bfd233ce-ad03-5aa7-ae93-8771601b093f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{16}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{16}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302629} {:answer/id #uuid "9f0224f7-0a9a-5336-9b68-f7f2db670634" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{16}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302630} {:answer/id #uuid "cc001abf-092a-5a1d-8390-d0d0b1eede7c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{16}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{36}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302631} {:answer/id #uuid "5f01f67a-d6f0-521e-9d97-e0e07d60595a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{12}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{32}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302632} {:answer/id #uuid "a970540f-7f5e-5533-bf59-409804d91b62" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{36}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{16}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302633}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cc001abf-092a-5a1d-8390-d0d0b1eede7c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{16}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{36}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302631} :answer-field/id #uuid "3866022d-6dc1-5ad6-9bb6-cb35feebc02d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302628}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "87523b7e-951d-5546-83a0-445b96188688" :question/math-academy-id "q-73627" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039348/assets/377a871e9328e0a8b3c12d8904ecc16a2e6e3a17fa7dba05925bb6f2e5d7e4ad.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the ellipse given above?" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the equation of an ellipse centered at the origin with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nHere, the horizontal radius has length $a=4$ and the vertical radius has length $b=6.$ Therefore, the equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{{4}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{6}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{16}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{36} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186302634 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4e43e393-8752-58bc-b87c-b72f679cbfd9" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Lengths of the Major and Minor Axes Given the Equation of an Ellipse"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c08e4441-1b85-548e-866f-0bbe91509b31" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$4\\sqrt{5}$ and $8$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302636} {:answer/id #uuid "01fb5785-3bfd-590e-bd98-4314caba8958" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$2\\sqrt{5}$ and $4$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302637} {:answer/id #uuid "49caabf1-8a45-5fb9-b285-5e0e6925936a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$20$ and $16$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302638} {:answer/id #uuid "b7b8ca2d-f57a-5836-9fbf-cd20e35e1328" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$10$ and $8$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302639} {:answer/id #uuid "afb0cc5f-207a-5937-90f5-43576789c062" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\sqrt{5}$ and $2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302640}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c08e4441-1b85-548e-866f-0bbe91509b31" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$4\\sqrt{5}$ and $8$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302636} :answer-field/id #uuid "e6eb3028-8a16-537e-abc8-0c81cc9ab9b8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302635}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e572cb8d-0721-59ec-897a-5e0fa685feb4" :question/math-academy-id "q-7597" :question/problem "What are the lengths of the major and minor axes of an ellipse with equation \n$\\frac{{x}^{2}}{20}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{16}=1?$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the equation of an ellipse centered at the origin with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nIn the given equation, we have ${a}^{2}=20$ and ${b}^{2}=16.$\n\n- Since ${a}^{2}=20,$ the length of the horizontal radius must be $a=\\sqrt{20}=2\\sqrt{5}.$\n\n- Since ${b}^{2}=16,$ the length of the vertical radius must be $b=\\sqrt{16}=4.$\n\nSo the semi-major axis has length $a=2\\sqrt{5},$ and the semi-minor axis has length $b=4.$\n\nTherefore, the major axis has length $2a=2\\cdot 2\\sqrt{5}=4\\sqrt{5},$ and the minor axis has length $2b=2\\cdot 4=8.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186302641 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4e43e393-8752-58bc-b87c-b72f679cbfd9" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Lengths of the Major and Minor Axes Given the Equation of an Ellipse"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "69780d0e-b47b-5857-a7d7-f64664effc32" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$25$ and $16$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302643} {:answer/id #uuid "40790eb2-65af-5829-965a-210ba1346ceb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$5$ and $4$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302644} {:answer/id #uuid "6c1598a7-1301-5a4a-aee2-bb877212da6a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$10$ and $8$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302645} {:answer/id #uuid "bb63ec74-31d9-5b97-bfd4-adb1557fc2da" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\sqrt{5}$ and $2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302646} {:answer/id #uuid "98359209-bf7e-5f57-bdca-7083b041eb2a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$50$ and $32$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302647}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6c1598a7-1301-5a4a-aee2-bb877212da6a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$10$ and $8$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302645} :answer-field/id #uuid "35a53f71-a2af-5674-b14e-2dd4603052c1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302642}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ac2c9003-5051-5900-b74a-13fbad11f3f1" :question/math-academy-id "q-7601" :question/problem "What are the lengths of the major and minor axes of an ellipse with equation \n$\\frac{{x}^{2}}{16}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{25}=1?$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the equation of an ellipse centered at the origin with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nIn the given equation, we have ${a}^{2}=16$ and ${b}^{2}=25.$\n\n- Since ${a}^{2}=16,$ the length of the horizontal radius must be $a=\\sqrt{16}=4.$\n\n- Since ${b}^{2}=25,$ the length of the vertical radius must be $b=\\sqrt{25}=5.$\n\nSo the semi-major axis has length $b=5,$ and the semi-minor axis has length $a=4.$\n\nTherefore, the major axis has length $2b=2\\cdot 5=10,$ and the minor axis has length $2a=2\\cdot 4=8.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186302648 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "de557d1d-5f27-50e3-bcba-22b21f83267f" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Equation of a Tall Ellipse"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7da27217-d247-55c1-a5c9-5af77e1e1c35" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{9}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{1}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302650} {:answer/id #uuid "fe97d4c5-5586-58cb-8a81-1d61e723af44" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{3}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{1}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302651} {:answer/id #uuid "b479ee9c-3778-54e1-ae5e-9f9f511e572b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302652} {:answer/id #uuid "60ac96ff-2016-5aa4-b95c-f6d708b92c38" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{1}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{3}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302653} {:answer/id #uuid "99d3d3c8-65af-5ea2-94d2-b0a2e9dbd4af" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{1}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302654}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "99d3d3c8-65af-5ea2-94d2-b0a2e9dbd4af" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{1}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302654} :answer-field/id #uuid "9f505143-94bd-519c-9792-9c423ea7f276" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302649}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "63a3a21a-2d2d-56d9-89d0-68504601e683" :question/math-academy-id "q-7602" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039348/assets/bcac8eb60e0603ee38bd200b15072685a2bcebb834d490fb4e5a0c318f401096.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the ellipse given above?" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the equation of an ellipse centered at the origin with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nHere, the horizontal radius has length $a=1$ and the vertical radius has length $b=3.$ Therefore, the equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{{1}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{3}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{1}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186088267 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f88c1deb-cd11-5b68-b90b-2d8edfae2469" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Equation of a Wide Ellipse"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8507f770-a69b-5092-a5b4-b79e0b098480" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9x^{2}}{24} + \\frac{y^{2}}{2} = 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186086534} {:answer/id #uuid "9e547128-8b00-5113-a6c1-111d4b09b43a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x^{2}}{4} + \\frac{y^{2}}{9} = 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186086535} {:answer/id #uuid "d62d34b4-17dc-56b1-a7ce-3027ad139467" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x^{2}}{9} + \\frac{y^{2}}{4} = 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186086536} {:answer/id #uuid "011eb451-c6fe-5263-b706-0180d30dc196" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4x^{2}}{49} + \\frac{y^{2}}{4} = 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186086537} {:answer/id #uuid "4baf49d2-91c2-5e4e-afdc-8f6bfb485b96" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2x^{2}}{7} + \\frac{y^{2}}{2} = 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186086538}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "011eb451-c6fe-5263-b706-0180d30dc196" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4x^{2}}{49} + \\frac{y^{2}}{4} = 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186086537} :answer-field/id #uuid "2f97fdf5-8790-5ae4-bdec-4c23339c2436" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186086533}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0f8eff0d-f84c-5907-a2c9-a5a7eb91d57f" :question/math-academy-id "q-7603" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039348/assets/8ac809353e7834d328d645fafb5c02e17386ba087e778a841865ef6313893e79.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the ellipse given above?" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the equation of an ellipse centered at the origin with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nHere, the horizontal radius has length $a=\\frac{7}{2}$ and the vertical radius has length $b=2.$ Therefore, the equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{{3.5}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{2}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{{(\\frac{7}{2})}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{(\\frac{{7}^{2}}{{2}^{2}})}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{(\\frac{49}{4})}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{4{x}^{2}}{49}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186088268 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f88c1deb-cd11-5b68-b90b-2d8edfae2469" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Equation of a Wide Ellipse"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "81292d50-5c51-5b38-89f0-949bc6b6a964" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x^{2}}{8} + \\frac{y^{2}}{2} = 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186086540} {:answer/id #uuid "0c18f3df-95fb-536c-8e2f-3029a38b2427" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x^{2}}{2} + \\frac{y^{2}}{4} = 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186086541} {:answer/id #uuid "1e67014b-0d00-54c0-af93-fd3ae84e9b33" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x^{2}}{4} + \\frac{y^{2}}{2} = 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186086542} {:answer/id #uuid "3c28a557-2851-503b-97be-c5d293379692" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x^{2}}{4} + \\frac{y^{2}}{16} = 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186086543} {:answer/id #uuid "7affd3de-ff29-5c52-853b-6c179253ff99" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x^{2}}{16} + \\frac{y^{2}}{4} = 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186086544}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7affd3de-ff29-5c52-853b-6c179253ff99" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x^{2}}{16} + \\frac{y^{2}}{4} = 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186086544} :answer-field/id #uuid "92982adf-0bda-5979-982f-53887542631a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186086539}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "808bb938-3f2e-5c94-82a4-205181f5d6ac" :question/math-academy-id "q-7604" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039348/assets/d2c35e72acad77ae747c6a78c9794e9b076c047891d4b12d5c9b3176bdc6dde5.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the ellipse given above?" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the equation of an ellipse centered at the origin with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nHere, the horizontal radius has length $a=4$ and the vertical radius has length $b=2.$ Therefore, the equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{{4}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{2}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{16}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
